# fuxi: device-side XNU patch series, GPU-free cut. 99 patches, in this order.
#
# Target: iOS 16.7.16 (20H392), xnu-8796.141.3, Darwin 22.6.0,
#         apple-oss-distributions/xnu @ 1b191cb58250d0705d8a51287127505aa4bc0789.
#
# Consumer: unixnu/scripts/unixnu/patches.py.plan() treats every non-comment line
# as a file name relative to this directory and prepare() runs `git apply` on it,
# in order, inside the XNU work tree. A line that is not a git-applyable patch
# aborts the kernel step, so the three stage scripts below cannot be listed here.
#
# Provenance
#   0001-0081  ios-sweet @ 45263be, xnu/patches. Byte-identical (81/81 `cmp`) to
#              the copies the old fuxi tree shipped, i.e. the exact combination
#              that reached SpringBoard on hardware. Copied, not re-derived.
#   0082-0113  fuxi's own layer from /home/mai/fuxi-build/src/xnu/patches
#              (0094 never existed; the old tree skips it).
#   The three 00xx-stage-*.sh next to this file are the dxb stage scripts from
#   the same directory, unchanged.
#
# Stage scripts MUST run in the work tree before the first patch. series cannot
# express them (see above), so they are named here and the invoking step has to
# execute them:
#   0019-stage-libpthread.sh  libpthread-514.100.2 @ a6c70ca0 -> bsd/pthread/sweet_libpthread
#                             required by 0019
#   0020-stage-bearssl.sh     BearSSL 7bea48e5 -> libkern/crypto/sweet_bearssl
#                             required by 0020, and by 0027/0032/0033 to compile
#   0026-stage-hfs.sh         hfs-627.100.6 @ 31d5ec23 -> bsd/sweet_hfs
#                             required by 0026, 0031, 0041, 0052
#   Environment: the scripts exit 0 without doing anything unless
#   MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET, and exit 1 unless MACOS_VERSION=13.5, so the caller must
#   export MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET MACOS_VERSION=13.5 (their SWEET guard is the dxb
#   convention; the staged sources are guarded by CONFIG_* and FUXI in the
#   patches, not by that name). They also copy TargetConditionals.h out of the
#   macOS SDK via `xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path`; on the Linux kernel path
#   that xcrun is the shim installed by scripts/linux/setup-toolchain.py. Each
#   script refuses to overwrite an existing target directory, so it is only safe
#   on a freshly prepared work tree, which is what patches.prepare() clones.
#   patches.py has no hook for them; integration proposal in the release report
#   (.cache/xnu-series-release.md): let plan() pass `.sh` entries through to
#   prepare(), which runs them with subprocess in the work tree before the loop.
#
# Excluded: 13 of the 31 fuxi patches (0082-0113). Seven are GPU by content, six are
# non-GPU patches whose hunk context is anchored on an excluded GPU patch (they
# do not apply with the GPU layer gone; they need a re-derivation, not fuzz).
#   0096-fuxi-adreno                 Adreno A740 driver + gpu.c/gpu-*.h, ABI, DCVS
#   0097-fuxi-touch-boost            CPU/touch boost; calls fuxi_gpu_access() and
#                                    fuxi_gpu_start() from the Adreno driver, and
#                                    its bsd/conf/files + SweetFramebuffer hunk
#                                    context is the fuxi_adreno.c line 0096 adds
#   0098-fuxi-native-adreno-abi      native Adreno/Metal ABI, FuxiAdrenoUserClient
#   0100-sweet-execswap-gpu-abi-trace GPU ABI trace; edits FuxiAdrenoUserClient.cpp(0098)
#   0101-fuxi-gpu-nc-cache-sync      pmap nc-alias sync for the GPU reservation
#   0102-fuxi-gpu-backboardd-open    FuxiAdrenoUserClient.cpp (0098) only
#   0108-fuxi-gpu-scanout            GPU scanout in SweetSurface + pe_serial
#   --- blocked by the cut, not GPU themselves ---
#   0099-fuxi-wlan    1 hunk of bsd/conf/files wants the `bsd/dev/fuxi_perf.c`
#                     line 0097 adds; everything else applies
#   0103-fuxi-kernel-h1  2 of 10 fuxi_keys.c hunks want 0097's fuxi_perf_input()
#   0104-fuxi-wifi-ios   2 conf-file hunks want 0097's fuxi_perf.c and 0098's
#                     FuxiAdrenoUserClient.cpp lines
#   0106-fuxi-unixnu     sweet_ufs.c/vfs hunks apply; 6+ SweetFramebuffer hunks are
#                     the GPU scanout path (needs 0096/0098/0108) -> split, GPU
#                     part out, non-GPU part re-derived
#   0107-fuxi-sys        5 of 7 sweet_amfi.c hunks want the 0103 edits
#   0109-fuxi-backlight  the single iokit/conf/files.arm64 hunk wants 0098's
#                     FuxiAdrenoUserClient.cpp line
#
# Ordering constraints inside the list (do not reorder): 0031 and 0041 only apply
# after the HFS stage; 0019 needs the libpthread stage; 0027/0032/0033 need the
# BearSSL stage to compile; 0022/0024/0052 follow 0021/0026; 0030/0034/0047/0054/
# 0069 follow 0028; 0043/0044/0055 follow 0038; 0056/0067/0068/0079 follow 0046.
#
# The three stage scripts are the first three entries, and patches.prepare() runs
# every ".sh" entry with bash in the work tree before it applies the next patch, so
# the staged sources exist by the time 0019/0020/0026 need them. They are gated by
# MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET and MACOS_VERSION=13.5, which this device declares in
# board.toml [kernel] patch_env; without them the scripts exit 0 and the patches
# below fail. A series entry that is a script is run, not applied.
#
# Verified: on a --depth 1 clone of the commit above, after running the three
# stage scripts, a patches.prepare()-equivalent loop (git apply --check, then
# git apply, no --fuzz, no -C, no 3-way) applied all 99 patches clean, in order,
# 99/99, and produced the same tree as an independent replay. Details and the
# per-patch result table: .cache/xnu-series-release.md.
# Digests for review (sha256):
#   cat of the 99 patches below, in this order
#     d2e0cd0ba26853a6e8f580b04b33ede889ac993d24e0f6ab64d5bf1fec7ad87c
